"Non-Commercial Use" means use by a natural person solely for their own
personal study, research, evaluation, testing or personal activities that
are not directed toward business operations, commercial advantage or
monetary compensation. Use for an employer, client, business, paid service
or revenue-generating activity is not Non-Commercial Use, including use
inside an organization even when the Software itself is not sold.

"Modified Work" means an altered version of the Software or a work derived
from it, including changes to source code, features or branding, ports,
translations of the Software, and incorporation of its original material
into another product. Compiling unchanged source using documented build
steps, installing dependencies, and changing ordinary runtime preferences
do not by themselves create a Modified Work. Independently created files
or Git repositories managed with the Software do not become Modified Works
merely through that use; the commercial-use restriction still applies to
the use of the Software itself.

